{
  "id": "praesens",
  "name": "Present tense: regular -ar, -er, -ir verbs",
  "level": "A1",
  "variety": "pt-PT",
  "ptBR": { "note": "Brazil writes falamos for both “we speak” and “we spoke”. In Portugal the past is falámos, with an accent." },
  "subtitle": "Portuguese verbs end in -ar, -er or -ir. Take off the ending and add the one for the person: falar → falo, falas, fala. Use the present for now, for habits and for facts.",
  "briefMarks": ["-ar", "-er", "-ir", "-o", "-as", "-es"],
  "source": "icanspeak Portuguese original text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-11-12)",
  "concept": {
    "qaWithTable": true,
    "flow": [
      { "text": "stem: fal-", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "ending: -o, -as, -a …", "variant": "verb" },
      { "text": "falo, falas, fala" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "Trabalh<span class=\"vp-verb\">o</span> num hotel. · Com<span class=\"vp-verb\">es</span> em casa? · Viv<span class=\"vp-verb\">emos</span> em Viseu. · Abr<span class=\"vp-verb\">imos</span> às nove.",
    "table": {
      "caption": "Present tense: the endings",
      "rows": [
        { "pron": "eu", "end": "-o" },
        { "pron": "tu", "end": "-as / -es" },
        { "pron": "ele, ela, o senhor, a senhora, você", "end": "-a / -e" },
        { "pron": "nós", "end": "-amos / -emos / -imos" },
        { "pron": "eles, elas, vocês", "end": "-am / -em" }
      ],
      "verbs": [
        { "inf": "falar", "forms": ["fal|o", "fal|as", "fal|a", "fal|amos", "fal|am"] },
        { "inf": "comer", "forms": ["com|o", "com|es", "com|e", "com|emos", "com|em"] },
        { "inf": "viver", "forms": ["viv|o", "viv|es", "viv|e", "viv|emos", "viv|em"] },
        { "inf": "abrir", "forms": ["abr|o", "abr|es", "abr|e", "abr|imos", "abr|em"] }
      ]
    },
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "Each ending shows the person, so you do not need <em>eu</em> or <em>tu</em>: <em>Falo português. Falas inglês?</em>",
        "tag": "The ending"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>-er</strong> and <strong>-ir</strong> verbs have the same endings, except <em>nós</em>: <em>comemos, bebemos</em> but <em>abrimos, partimos</em>. Careful: <em>viver</em> is an <em>-er</em> verb: <em>vivemos</em>.",
        "tag": "-er and -ir"
      },
      {
        "html": "The present is for <strong>habits</strong>, <strong>facts</strong> and plans: <em>Ao domingo almoço com a minha mãe. Moro em Faro. Amanhã trabalho em casa.</em> For something happening right now, Portugal says <em>estou a trabalhar</em> (more at A2).",
        "tag": "When"
      },
      {
        "html": "To say “not”, put <strong>não</strong> before the verb: <em>Não falo alemão.</em> There is no word like <em>do</em>: <em>Trabalhas hoje?</em>",
        "tag": "não"
      },
      {
        "html": "The <em>nós</em> form of <em>-ar</em> verbs has no accent in the present: <em>falamos</em> (we speak). In Portugal <em>falámos</em>, with an accent, means “we spoke”.",
        "tag": "falamos"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>Eu falar português</em> → ✓ <em>Falo português</em>. ✗ <em>Ela vivo aqui</em> → ✓ <em>Ela vive aqui</em>. ✗ <em>Vivimos em Lisboa</em> → ✓ <em>Vivemos em Lisboa</em> (<em>viver</em> is an <em>-er</em> verb). For Spanish speakers: the <em>eles</em> form ends in <em>-am / -em</em> (<em>falam, comem</em>), not <em>-an / -en</em>. Other verbs change more: <a href=\"/present-irregular\">Key irregular verbs</a> and <a href=\"/vowel-change-verbs\">Verbs that change in the eu form</a>.",
    "reference": {
      "showLabel": "Show overview ▼",
      "hideLabel": "Hide overview ▲",
      "tables": [
        {
          "caption": "Regular verbs to learn first",
          "head": ["-ar", "-er", "-ir"],
          "rows": [
            ["falar (speak)", "comer (eat)", "abrir (open)"],
            ["trabalhar (work)", "beber (drink)", "partir (leave, break)"],
            ["morar (live, reside)", "viver (live)", "decidir (decide)"],
            ["estudar (study)", "aprender (learn)", "assistir (watch, attend)"],
            ["comprar (buy)", "vender (sell)", "discutir (discuss)"],
            ["pagar (pay)", "perceber (understand)", "existir (exist)"]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "boxes": [
        {
          "badge": "Careful: three endings for nós",
          "variant": "dat",
          "items": [
            "falar → falamos",
            "comer → comemos, viver → vivemos",
            "abrir → abrimos"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  },
